# The CI base image the toolchain prefix is composed onto.
#
# The toolshed supplies the language runtimes the test suite needs -- Go, Rust,
# Node, Python -- which the toolchain images deliberately do not carry. The
# composed image is what ci.yml runs in.
#
# ci.yml names the composed tag literally, because a workflow's container image
# is resolved before any step could read this file. If the two disagree the
# image will not exist and the job fails at container pull, which is loud.
# Changing this line means changing that tag too.
ghcr.io/opencyphal/toolshed:ts26.4.3
